    "body": "## Summary\n\nReplaces ADR-031's block-level narrowing (LTR) with per-line float-aware wrapping. Implements the fix ADR-079 prescribed and closes the History-position defect at the layout level.\n\n- `FloatContext` in `layout.cpp` (anonymous namespace) carries parent content geometry + float reserves into `layout_element` as an optional trailing arg. Header change: none — `layout()` / `layout_with_pseudo()` signatures unchanged.\n- `LineWidthProvider` + `LineWidth` added to `text_utils.hpp`. Both `break_into_lines` and `break_styled_words_into_lines` accept an optional provider + `starting_y`; empty provider preserves pre-ADR-079 behavior byte-for-byte.\n- `LineFragment::x_offset` carries the per-line left indent (0 outside any float).\n- `layout_block_children` builds a local `FloatContext` when a child starts within a float's y-range; hands it to `layout_element`. RTL retains block-narrowing as a scoped fallback.\n- `flush_inline_run` builds the provider lambda against `content_x` / `content_w`; wraps to absolute y before passing to the breakers.\n\n## Expected impact\n\nWikipedia `<h2>History` should move from `y≈2210` to `y≈500–600` at 984px content width. Bug A (infobox at wrong y) and Bug B (paragraph stretch) resolve together since they share the root cause.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- [x] `cmake --build build --target honeybee_tests -j1` — clean\n- [x] `./build/tests/honeybee_tests \"[adr079]\"` — 6/6, 25 assertions\n- [x] `./build/tests/honeybee_tests` — **3017 assertions in 764 test cases, all passing**\n- [x] Updated 5 pre-existing tests whose assertions depended on block-level narrowing. Their intent is preserved (floats still narrow to their expected widths — ADR-066 intrinsic / Layer-2 cap / explicit width — and ADR-031's placement/`cursor_y` invariants still hold).\n- [ ] **Manual**: load Wikipedia's HTML article at default width, confirm History is at `y≈500` (follow-up, not blocking merge)\n\n## What this does NOT do\n\n- RTL: block-narrowing retained (documented fallback). Arabic pages' behavior is unchanged.\n- Multi-level float interaction (local float takes precedence over ancestor float; not summed). Wikipedia's History case is single-level.\n- No retry on the transition line — `y_top < float_bottom` picks the width, matching Firefox.\n",
    "closed_at": "2026-11-24T05:25:47Z",
